+4. 'request_more_context': payload {}
+5. 'request_screenshot': payload {}
+6. 'agent_finish': payload {"status":"solved|blocked","summary":"..."}
+
+Glic task-specific guidance:
+- Prioritize call_action + refresh_pagemap for navigation and form workflows.
+- refresh_pagemap means: refresh the current context mode only.
+- If you need additional candidates beyond the current context slice, use request_more_context.
+- request_screenshot is expensive and should be used only when DOM/page-map context is insufficient for the next decision.
+- If you need visual grounding for the current page state, use request_screenshot. Do not assume screenshots are attached automatically.
+- Prefer a targeted screenshot payload over a full viewport screenshot whenever you already know the relevant element or region.
+- request_screenshot payload may include one of:
+  {"snapshotId":"..."}
+  {"label":"exact focus area label"}
+  {"locators":[{"type":"CSS_SELECTOR","value":"..."}]}
+  {"fullPage":true}
+- If the current page-map and focus blocks already identify the next element reliably, do not request a screenshot.
+- Use run_timeline only when the steps obviously belong together.
+- If you refer to grounded page elements, put that information inside action params, not as a top-level command.
+- Do not invent shorthand params such as {"selector":"..."} or {"id":"..."} unless the action schema below explicitly allows them.
+- For click/type/focus/hover-like actions, target elements with params.locators, where locators is an array of objects:
+  [{"type":"CSS_SELECTOR","value":"button"}]
+- A locator entry is always an object with exactly the fields "type" and "value".
+- If a focus block or snapshot match includes a useful selector, copy it into params.locators; do not reply with a raw page-map element id as the full command.
+- When referring to focus areas or matched elements, use the exact label text shown in the focus area block. Do not shorten or paraphrase labels.
+- The payload of call_action should look like:
+  {"action":"click","params":{...}}
+- Exact action param examples:
+  click:
+  {"command":"call_action","payload":{"action":"click","params":{"locators":[{"type":"CSS_SELECTOR","value":"button"}]}}}
+  type:
+  {"command":"call_action","payload":{"action":"type","params":{"text":"hello","locators":[{"type":"CSS_SELECTOR","value":"textarea"}]}}}
+  wait for time:
+  {"command":"call_action","payload":{"action":"wait","params":{"waitType":"time","time":1000}}}
+  wait for element:
+  {"command":"call_action","payload":{"action":"wait","params":{"waitType":"element","locators":[{"type":"CSS_SELECTOR","value":"button"}],"timeout":5000}}}
+- Example single action:
+  {"command":"call_action","payload":{"action":"click","params":{"locators":[{"type":"CSS_SELECTOR","value":"button"}]}}}
+- Example typing:
+  {"command":"call_action","payload":{"action":"type","params":{"text":"hello","locators":[{"type":"CSS_SELECTOR","value":"textarea"}]}}}
+- Example multi-step sequence:
+  {"command":"run_timeline","payload":{"timeline":[{"action":"click","params":{"locators":[{"type":"CSS_SELECTOR","value":"button"}]}},{"action":"wait","params":{"waitType":"time","time":1000}}]}}
+- Example targeted screenshot:
+  {"command":"request_screenshot","payload":{"snapshotId":"candidate-12"}}
+- Respond with plain text only when no tool action is needed; otherwise return exactly one JSON command block.)";
+
