@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+# Simulachrome Stash Reconciliation
+
+Working reference for `stash-backup-patch-only-20260423` vs current
+`simulachrome_m144_apply`.
+
+Status labels:
+- `KEEP`: current M144 branch behavior is the intended direction
+- `PORT`: stash had useful behavior not fully reintegrated yet
+- `DROP`: stash behavior conflicts with the current trusted/native direction or is superseded
+
+## Native Input / Runtime
+
+- `KEEP` `chrome/browser/ui/webui/dashboard/actions/type_handler.cc`
+  Current native type path is the right direction. Keep browser-side trusted typing.
+- `PORT` `chrome/browser/ui/webui/dashboard/actions/type_handler.cc`
+  Stabilize delayed typing callbacks and minimize copied `ResolvedElement` state.
+- `KEEP` `chrome/browser/ui/webui/dashboard/actions/key_press_action.cc`
+  Dual native/CDP key press support and proper `Tab` behavior belong in current.
+- `PORT` `chrome/browser/ui/webui/dashboard/click_handler.cc`
+  Keep stash’s safer force-activation gating and overlay context validation.
+- `KEEP` `chrome/browser/ui/webui/dashboard/actions/action_factory.cc`
+  Routed action creation plus runtime failover is the target design.
+
+## Listener / Runtime Control
+
+- `KEEP` `chrome/browser/ui/webui/dashboard/actions/listen_action.cc`
+  Keep native snapshot + CDP dual backend direction.
+- `DROP` renderer JS observer path and Blink listener side-channel hooks
+  They conflict with the trusted/native direction and create merge-hostile upstream drift.
+- `PORT` `chrome/browser/ui/webui/dashboard/listener_manager.cc`
+  Keep parity-related routing and persistence improvements where still missing.
+- `KEEP` `chrome/browser/ui/webui/dashboard/ui_messages/dashboard_ui_message_handler_listener.cc`
+  Current modularized listener UI message split is better than the old monolith.
+
+## Glic / Context Pipeline
+
+- `KEEP` `chrome/browser/ui/webui/dashboard/unified_page_context.cc`
+  Current branch already routes dashboard page-map acquisition through Glic-native context.
+- `KEEP` `chrome/browser/glic/agent/unified_agent_*`
+  These are part of the intended unified agent direction. Do not delete them.
+- `DROP` stash-side deletion of unified agent files
+  Current branch is correct to keep them.
+- `KEEP` current `chrome/browser/glic/*` and `chrome/browser/resources/glic/*` parity where head-vs-stash is already identical or better
+  No remaining targeted stash port is needed there unless a new concrete feature gap appears.
+
+## Recorder / Targeting / UX
+
+- `PORT` `chrome/browser/ui/webui/dashboard/recorder_controller.cc`
+  Resource-tree locator capture and guided visual fallback are useful and aligned with metadata soft locators.
+- `KEEP` `chrome/browser/resources/dashboard/components/locatorEditor.js`
+  Current editor is already effectively aligned with stash for locator management.
+- `KEEP` `chrome/browser/resources/dashboard/components/dashboard_timeline_renderer.js`
+  Current timeline preview path is already close enough; no priority stash gap remains.
+- `PORT` `chrome/browser/resources/dashboard/actions/scrapeTableEditor.js`
+  Clearer UX, examples, previews, and field-expansion visibility are worth keeping.
+
+## Headless Fallback / Parity
+
+- `KEEP` native-headless routed execution as the primary debuggable path
+  This is the headed/headless parity target.
+- `PORT` `chrome/browser/resources/dashboard/headless_listener_host.py`
+  Keep only emergency-fallback improvements that help parity:
+  - scroll actions in key scripts
+  - listener initial/refresh scroll controls
+  - explicit window size / device scale factor
+  - transition conditions like `new_child` / `new_child_contains`
+- `DROP` old dashboard AI stream plumbing from the Python host
+  That path was tied to legacy dashboard console flows that are already being retired.
+
+## Scrape Table
+
+- `KEEP` native/page-map implementation
+  This matches the trusted execution direction better than adding a scrape-specific CDP branch.
+- `PORT` stash native backend improvements
+  - row index list/range support
+  - nth-child/nth-of-type field expansion
+  - header-derived field naming
+  - stronger row/field matching
+  - smarter CSV naming
+- `DROP` stash semantic JS fallback unless a concrete native gap forces it later
+
+## Dashboard UI Message Handler
+
+- `KEEP` modularization
+  The large diff is mostly expected because current split listener handling into dedicated files.
+- `DROP` any stash-only monolithic reversion
+  Current split-file structure is the right direction.
